\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Definition-sensitive information retention on the regular centralizer torsor. Panel A separates the point-order/fixed-point Burnside construction of 2008, the labelled $\mathbb  Z\!\times \!G$ carrier of 2013, the orbit-order and orbifold constructions of 2015, and the enhanced carrier of 2018 \cite  {GuseinZadeLuengoMelle2008,GuseinZade2013,GuseinZadeLuengoMelle2015,EbelingGuseinZade2018}. Panel B records which information each named carrier retains; the rows are distinct established constructions, not a universal dominance order. Panel C gives the four frozen scalar reductions. In particular, point-cardinality has support $r_q$, exponent $m_q$, and unit exponent when $m_q=1$. The star marks the sole locked exception $q=2$, where $(r_2,m_2)=(3,1)$; because $r_2=r_4=3$, this coincidence is not modulus-specific. The certified negative statement is only family-uniform: no one scalar-reduction type combines source support and unit exponent over all nine locked rows.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:retention-hierarchy}{{1}{4}{Definition-sensitive information retention on the regular centralizer torsor. Panel A separates the point-order/fixed-point Burnside construction of 2008, the labelled $\mathbb Z\!\times \!G$ carrier of 2013, the orbit-order and orbifold constructions of 2015, and the enhanced carrier of 2018 \cite {GuseinZadeLuengoMelle2008,GuseinZade2013,GuseinZadeLuengoMelle2015,EbelingGuseinZade2018}. Panel B records which information each named carrier retains; the rows are distinct established constructions, not a universal dominance order. Panel C gives the four frozen scalar reductions. In particular, point-cardinality has support $r_q$, exponent $m_q$, and unit exponent when $m_q=1$. The star marks the sole locked exception $q=2$, where $(r_2,m_2)=(3,1)$; because $r_2=r_4=3$, this coincidence is not modulus-specific. The certified negative statement is only family-uniform: no one scalar-reduction type combines source support and unit exponent over all nine locked rows}{figure.1}{}}
\citation{GuseinZadeLuengoMelle2015}
